# Alert

Shows a short, important message without interrupting the user. Compose it from `Alert`, an optional icon, `AlertTitle`, `AlertDescription`, and `AlertAction`. The root sets `role="alert"`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Alert, AlertTitle, AlertDescription } from "#lib/components/ui/alert/index.js";
	import { CircleCheckIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Alert>
	<CircleCheckIcon />
	<AlertTitle>Success! Your changes have been saved</AlertTitle>
	<AlertDescription>This is an alert with an icon, title, and description.</AlertDescription>
</Alert>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/alert.json
```

## Icon

Place an icon as the first child of `Alert`. It gets a leading column beside the title and description, and inherits the alert's text color. Without an icon, the text fills the full width.

## Destructive

Set `variant="destructive"` to tint the text, icon, and description with the destructive color. `AlertDescription` can hold several paragraphs.

<Demo section="destructive" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Alert, AlertTitle, AlertDescription } from "#lib/components/ui/alert/index.js";
	import { CircleAlertIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Alert variant="destructive">
	<CircleAlertIcon />
	<AlertTitle>Unable to process your payment.</AlertTitle>
	<AlertDescription>
		<p>Please verify your billing information and try again.</p>
		<p>Check your card details, ensure sufficient funds, and verify your billing address.</p>
	</AlertDescription>
</Alert>
```

## Action

Place `AlertAction` last inside `Alert` to show trailing content, such as a button. It sits in a final column beside the title and description.

<Demo section="action" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Alert, AlertTitle, AlertDescription, AlertAction } from "#lib/components/ui/alert/index.js";
	import { Button } from "#lib/components/ui/button/index.js";
	import { InfoIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Alert>
	<InfoIcon />
	<AlertTitle>A new version is available</AlertTitle>
	<AlertDescription>Reload the page to get the latest features.</AlertDescription>
	<AlertAction>
		<Button size="sm" variant="outline">Reload</Button>
	</AlertAction>
</Alert>
```

## Size

Set `size` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the padding, gap, text, and icon size. It defaults to `lg`.

<Demo section="size" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Alert size="xs">
	<InfoIcon />
	<AlertTitle>Size xs</AlertTitle>
	<AlertDescription>A compact alert for forms and inline messages.</AlertDescription>
</Alert>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius, which follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill and can clip tall content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round corners that stay safe.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Alert rounded="3xl">
	<InfoIcon />
	<AlertTitle>Rounded 3xl</AlertTitle>
</Alert>
```

## API

The `Alert` props extend the native `div` attributes, and so do `AlertTitle`, `AlertDescription`, and `AlertAction`. Extra attributes and event handlers such as `onclick` pass through to each element.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Visual style of the alert */
	variant?: "default" | "destructive";
	/** Padding, gap, text, and icon size on the shared scale; defaults to `lg` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill that can clip the content, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
